; Put the first object into (or onto) the second
;
; Verb handler of the commands "drop in" (14) and "put in" (17) in the verb
; tables of containers (the second object); #R$8F69 also reaches it through
; #R$9F4A with the nouns swapped. It refuses, in this order:
; .
; #R$8D25 refuses first (the object has several places, like a door, or is a
; liquid); then "I cannot do that." when the first object is already in the
; second; "<container> is closed" (#R$A164) unless the container is open (this
; check is skipped for command 18, "put on"); and the message "<obj2> is too full."
; when the first object's weight (+2) is more than the container's capacity (+2)
; or does not leave room beside what it already holds (#R$9CE8; an exact fit is
; refused too).
; .
; Otherwise (CommitOrAbort: only when performed) the first object's holder (+1)
; becomes the second object and its location (+$10) becomes the container's.
;
; Noun1Record Record of the first object
; Noun2Record Record of the second object (the container)
; FirstObject Id of the first object
; SecondObject Id of the second object
; CommandId The command (14, 17 or 18)
@label=PutObjectIn
c$924F CALL $8D25        ; refuse a fixed object or a liquid
 $9252 LD A,($B6E9)      ;
 $9255 CP (IX+$01)       ; already in it?
 $9258 JP Z,$72CE        ; "I cannot do that."
 $925B LD IY,($B70A)     ; the container
 $925F LD A,($B6E7)      ;
@isub=CP CMD_PUT_ON
 $9262 CP $12            ; put on: no need for it to be open
 $9264 JR Z,$926C        ;
@isub=BIT FLAG_ACTIVE,(IY+$07)
 $9266 BIT 5,(IY+$07)    ; open?
 $926A JR Z,$9297        ;
*$926C LD A,(IY+$02)     ; container's capacity
 $926F SUB (IX+$02)      ; minus the weight of the object
 $9272 JR C,$927E        ; too heavy for it
 $9274 PUSH AF          ;
 $9275 LD A,($B6E9)      ;
 $9278 CALL $9CE8        ; weight it already holds
 $927B LD B,A            ;
 $927C POP AF            ;
 $927D SUB B             ; room left; carry or zero: too full
*$927E LD HL,$AE1A       ; "<obj2> is too full."
 $9281 JP C,$72DD        ;
 $9284 JP Z,$72DD        ;
 $9287 CALL $9D44        ; abandon unless performing
 $928A LD A,(IY+$10)     ; the object goes to the container's location
 $928D LD (IX+$10),A     ;
 $9290 LD A,($B6E9)      ; and its holder is the container
 $9293 LD (IX+$01),A     ;
 $9296 RET               ;
@isub=LD A,REASON_CLOSED
*$9297 LD A,$05          ; state "closed"
 $9299 JP $A164          ; "<container> is closed"
